# vim at the prompt, and history search.
Shot keys
Alt the prompt in vim's normal mode, marked gluon[n]>, with a block cursor on the line being edited
Also keys-search ctrl-r searching the history for bench, the matching line highlighted
Caption vim keys at the prompt when you want them, and ctrl-r through every line you have ever typed.
Config input.mode vim
History :t strconv.Atoi("12")
History :bench strconv.Itoa(n), fmt.Sprint(n)
History :layout pricing.LineItem
History n := 42
Grid 72x10
Line x := []string{"go", "gluon"}
Type `strings.Join(x, ", ")`
Esc
Type "bb"
Wait Prompt
Screenshot
Ctrl c
Wait Prompt
Ctrl r
Type "bench"
Wait Prompt
Screenshot keys-search
